From b0e152cf49495cc5981a74126401cbffd90d52d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 14:18:11 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] kcm_kscreen: display panels built on first use, titled
 sections, priority dialog on demand, busy state
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Page type: Device-like (screens are peers; the arrangement view stays the main control, one panel per display below it),
docs/page-design.md. KScreen config handling, OutputModel roles, kwinrc/KScreen settings, KAuth/D-Bus calls and the HDR
calibrator launch are unchanged. NOT BUILT YET (owner stopped heavy work; kscreen is empty under weston anyway);
checked statically only.

Moved / renamed:
- The per-display form was one flat group of ~25 rows. Now: an untitled first group (Display: Enabled, Primary or Change
  Screen Priorities…, Resolution, Refresh rate, Adaptive sync, Scale, Orientation, Replica of), then groups with noun titles,
  each shown only when the display supports something in it: "Image" (Overscan, RGB range, Sharpness), "Color" (color
  profile, ICC path/picker, color accuracy, color resolution limit, sRGB intensity), "High dynamic range" (HDR,
  Calibrate HDR Brightness…, EDR), "Brightness" (DDC/CI, brightness, adapt to environment, adaptive backlight modulation).
  Refresh rate moved up next to Resolution (it was after Scale and Orientation); Adaptive sync moved beside it; Replica of
  moved from the bottom to the first group. The global part (Legacy applications (X11), Screen tearing) got the group
  title "All displays".
- Wording: "Device:" -> "Display:" (the checkbox is still "Enabled"), "Enable HDR" -> "Use high dynamic range (HDR)",
  "Enable EDR" -> "Use extended dynamic range (EDR)" (no "Enable" prefix; their labels were dropped as the group title
  says it), "High/Extended Dynamic Range:" and "Adaptive Backlight Modulation:" -> sentence case.
- Nothing removed. Old wording added to the page aliases in ia/layout.json. Relabel table: inventory/relabel/kcm_kscreen.tsv
  (outer repo). Inventory --strict: 40 rows ok, 0 lost (markers on every control); full check LOST 0.
- HIG ids: HIG-001, HIG-005, HIG-006, HIG-057; page-design sections 2, 3, 7. ia/duplicates.md: Scale owner stays here.

Speed (cause found in code, not measured):
- Panel.qml's Repeater created an OutputPanel for EVERY display as soon as the config arrived, and each panel
  instantiates all its entries even when hidden (Kirigami.FormEntry visible:false still builds its control): about 40 controls
  per display including two ColorProfileSelectors, two IccSelectors (text field + file dialog launcher), five slider/spinbox
  pairs and the bits-per-color combo. A three-display setup built ~120 controls in one frame, only one of them visible.
  The model roles resolutions/refreshRates (output_model.cpp resolutionsStrings/resolutions: all modes, de-duplicated,
  sorted, formatted with a gcd per size) are rebuilt on every read from QML (model: element.resolutions plus
  element.resolutions[0] in the label), for each panel.
- Now: each display's panel is a Loader (asynchronous, active once the display has been selected, kept afterwards), so a
  config with N displays builds one panel; the others when their tab is clicked. OutputPanel takes `required property var
  element` (the delegate's model object) instead of reading the delegate context.
- The "Change Priorities" Kirigami.Dialog (and its measuring items) is a Loader built on first use; the enabled-outputs proxy
  model moved to the page root so the panels do not depend on the dialog.
- Before the backend answers the page was blank; now a BusyIndicator shows after 150 ms (Timer), and the error banner still
  covers a missing backend.
- Not changed: KCMKScreen::doSave() still blocks in SetConfigOperation::exec() (kcm.cpp, deliberate: the module may exit
  before an async operation completes, see its comment); GetConfigOperation is already asynchronous.
- After numbers: pending, manager will measure.

Not built yet; uncertain: `required property var model` in a Repeater/Loader delegate for a QSortFilterProxyModel (should
give the roles object as before); Loader implicit size feeding StackLayout's `children[currentIndex].implicitHeight`
while the asynchronous panel is incubating (page height may jump once); FormGroup `visible` driven by its entries' ids
(FormGroup is an Item, the entries' `visible` is the declared one not the effective one); Kirigami.Dialog opened from
Component.onCompleted inside a Loader and destroyed from onClosed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
